<section class="sec" id="why">
<div class="wrap">
<span class="eyebrow reveal">Why now</span>
<h2 class="st reveal">Why generative AI, and <span class="serif">why now.</span></h2>
<p class="lede reveal">Generative AI created a new layer of jobs almost overnight: people who wire LLMs into business workflows, build assistants over company knowledge and automate what teams do by hand. Those roles reward builders, and building is a learnable, four-month skill.</p>
<div class="why-stats">
<div class="ws reveal"><b>New</b><span class="t">Job family since 2023</span><p>AI engineer, prompt specialist and automation builder roles barely existed before.</p></div>
<div class="ws reveal"><b>80%</b><span class="t">Firms piloting GenAI</span><p>Nearly every enterprise is piloting; someone local has to build it.</p></div>
<div class="ws reveal"><b>No-code</b><span class="t">Half the opportunity</span><p>Automation platforms mean non-developers ship real AI systems too.</p></div>
</div>
<h3 class="reveal" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:800;font-size:1.2rem;margin-top:44px">Why it is a smart move for you</h3>
<div class="diff-grid" style="margin-top:22px">
<div class="diff reveal"><span class="ic-badge"><svg class="ic"><use href="#i-cap"></use></svg></span><b>Two tracks in one</b><p>Code-based LLM apps and no-code automation, so any background can build.</p></div>
